  "scope": "Paper45 only: two d(y) to d_{i}(y) repairs and one f(0,y) to f_{i}(0,y) repair; preserve every outside byte and both adjudicated KEEP readings.",
  "summary": "Mirror the activated German ED0015 three-token Paper45 notation correction into the current Ukrainian component without changing prose, producers, builds, or publication state.",
  "human_companion_path": "decision_records/UK001-EDIT-0014.md",
  "human_auditable_considerations": {
    "accepted": [
      "The common divisor belongs to the indexed f_i,g_i family and is already d_i(y) in both defining factorizations and the following noncongruence.",
      "The G construction must multiply by that same indexed divisor.",
      "The equation-(1) identity requires the coefficient f_i(0,y), paired with g_i(0,y) and the factors f_i,g_i."
    ],
    "rejected": [
      "Keep one or both bare d(y) readings, because that leaves an undefined or inconsistent divisor index.",
      "Introduce a new abbreviation or rewrite the proof, because either exceeds the admitted three-token repair.",
      "Rename the overloaded P or replace h_i y^(K) with an earlier lambda, because both are settled diplomatic KEEP readings."
    ],
    "claim_boundary": "Project-authority notation fidelity only; no native-language validation, community certification, or critical-edition claim."
  },
